// @run
// @log 2
// @log 5
// A `Set`'s `.values()` ARE its elements, and the BOUND form (`const xs = s.values()`)
// builds them through the key-list path — so it needs the key-list frame, which a Set
// receiver reserves for neither arm of the reservation ladder: a Set's shape is neither
// the mono `-1` nor an mv slot. A Set has no `.keys()` surface at all, so this is the
// ONLY bound list form a Set has.
//
// The i32-keyed Set reserves it (its `-5` sentinel is a new arm, so nothing pre-existing
// can move) and this is the pin. The STRING-keyed twin is still a loud reject —
// `emitProgram: .keys() but string list type not collected` for
// `const sv = s.values()` over a `{[string]: boolean}` Set — and is deliberately left
// alone: the reservation scan fires on every `.values()` call INCLUDING a
// `for v in s.values()` iterable, which needs no frame, so teaching the string half here
// grows two existing modules (`basics.vl`, `infer-from-add.vl`) for no behavior change.
// FILED, with the fix shape: the reservation has to distinguish the BOUND call from the
// for-in iterable, which the collect scan cannot see from the call node alone.
const t: {[i32]: boolean} = Set()
t.add(4)
t.add(5)
const tv = t.values()
print(tv.length) // 2
print(tv[1])     // 5
